, given a dataset consisting of historical trading records, bidding and market response, it first constructs the supply and demand forecasts in the empirical and LSTM sets. Then through a proper choice of the bidding strategy (29), the agent finally decides its bidding price at time t{t}
. After the agent submits its bidding price into the auction market and the new market response occurs, this pair will be recorded and added to the historical dataset. The mixture model aggregates the merits of these two estimators and provides a better estimation. We will compare these bidding strategies in the case study.
